2024Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodAxis_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodThreeMember_siRS1_e94UKDHG_yiiDCTQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:DebtInstrumentPrepaymentPremiumPercentage" scale="-2" id="Tc_JepnJdbFKkyc2EWGdXj8YA_4_3">0.00</ix:nonFraction>%</p></td></tr></table></div></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;min-height:0.0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:0pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:12pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Borrower was required to make scheduled quarterly amortization payments in an aggregate principal amount equal to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_batl_RatioToBeMaintainedForEachQuarterAfterJuneMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2024Member_mR4V5QpEtU60IynvCtAqxQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:DebtInstrumentQuarterlyAmortizationPaymentsPercent" scale="-2" id="Narr_YvFLM9vtWkO9ge43FI3bwg">2.50</ix:nonFraction>% of the total aggregate principal amount of the loans outstanding and such payments commenced the fiscal quarter ending June 30, 2025. </p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">16</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:36.7pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">BATTALION OIL CORPORATION</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">NOTES TO THE UNAUDITED CONDENSED CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS (continued)</b></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_Vc6cIfTtcUeJI6el0u8I8w_cont4" continuedAt="Tb_Vc6cIfTtcUeJI6el0u8I8w_cont5"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Under the 2024 Amended Term Loan Agreement, the Borrower could have been required to make mandatory prepayments of the loans in connection with the incurrence of non-permitted debt, certain asset sales and with excess cash on hand in excess of certain maximum levels. Accordingly, upon closing the West Quito Divestiture, the Company used $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_wpAg_pixNk6daaxK7TuvSw" contextRef="Duration_2_24_2026_To_2_24_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2024Member_Kw3F2CAbD0aFtXX14G3DIg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RepaymentsOfDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_OSlNt4063kCNygNgaKTbEQ">45.6</ix:nonFraction> million of the net proceeds from closing to repay amounts outstanding under the 2024 Amended Term Loan Agreement on February 24, 2026 including $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_wpAg_pixNk6daaxK7TuvSw" contextRef="Duration_2_24_2026_To_2_24_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2024Member_Kw3F2CAbD0aFtXX14G3DIg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:MandatoryPrepayment" scale="6" id="Narr_gMOznEp_qk--R9xFaTYcaQ">40.0</ix:nonFraction> million pursuant to the Third Amendment and prepayment of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_wpAg_pixNk6daaxK7TuvSw" contextRef="Duration_2_24_2026_To_2_24_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2024Member_Kw3F2CAbD0aFtXX14G3DIg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EarlyRepaymentOfSeniorDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_6kR52MlXckOmURtpHuLssQ">5.6</ix:nonFraction> million for the scheduled quarterly amortization payment for the quarterly period ending March 31, 2026.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:12pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In conjunction with entering into the 2024 Term Loan Agreement, the Company agreed to pay an exit fee equal to the amount resulting from multiplying <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2024Member_LjVw7OE94EKG7gNrnW3GTA" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:DebtInstrumentExitFeeComputationMultiplier" scale="-2" id="Narr_WHdInakgTkOQEt70hd6xrg">3.50</ix:nonFraction>% by the difference, if any, of (x) Total proved developed producing (&#8220;PDP&#8221;) PV-10 (the &#8220;PDP PV-10&#8221;) as of the date that is the earlier of (i)&#160;Payment in Full, (ii)&#160;the Maturity Date, or (iii)&#160;the loans and other obligations otherwise becoming immediately due and payable pursuant to Section 10.02 of the 2024 Term Loan Agreement (including whether, in the case of clauses (i) or (iii), such Payment in Full or acceleration, respectively, may be made in connection with a refinancing transaction or a disposition of all or substantially all of the assets of the Company) (such earlier date, the &#8220;Exit Fee Determination Date&#8221;), less (y) the Total PDP PV-10 reflected in the Initial Reserve Report after pro forma adjustment(s) for the West Quito Divestiture and any other disposition permitted by the credit agreement of otherwise consented to by the lenders (as defined in the 2024 Term Loan Agreement and as amended by the Third Amendment) (the &#8220;Exit Fee&#8221;). Upon evaluation of the payoff profiles associated with the Exit Fee, the Company concluded that such embedded features resulting from the application of this fee were not clearly and closely related to the host debt instrument. The fair value analysis for such derivative was performed and the fair value was deemed to be <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_wpAg_pixNk6daaxK7TuvSw" contextRef="As_Of_3_31_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreementMember_yHkpbnCB6k6ob0pYObEGZQ" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:DerivativeLiabilities" scale="0" id="Narr_mMFVzfWN80eGWJisS46tMw"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_wpAg_pixNk6daaxK7TuvSw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreementMember_S81MOuINk0iad22_6atpug" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:DerivativeLiabilities" scale="0" id="Narr_oGZg7F_zXkWuu4R01dgJPw">zero</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> at commencement, March 31, 2026 and at December 31, 2025. The Exit Fee derivative was not included in the 2026 Term Loan Agreement (defined below). Refer to Note 6, &#8220;<i style="font-style:italic;">Fair Value Measurements</i>,&#8221; for a discussion of the valuation approach used and the significant inputs to the valuation for the Exit Fee derivative.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">2026 Term Loan Agreement</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On June 30, 2026 (the &#8220;Closing Date&#8221;), Halc&#243;n Holdings, LLC (the &#8220;Borrower&#8221;), a wholly-owned subsidiary of the Company, entered into a Third Amended and Restated Senior Secured Credit Agreement (the &#8220;2026 Term Loan Agreement&#8221;), by and among the Company, the Borrower, the subsidiary guarantors party thereto, Fortress, as administrative agent, and certain other financial institutions party thereto, as lenders. The 2026 Term Loan Agreement amends and restates in its entirety the 2024 Amended Term Loan Agreement (defined above). All secured obligations under the 2024 Amended Term Loan Agreement were deemed continued and re-evidenced under the 2026 Term Loan Agreement. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:12pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Pursuant to the 2026 Term Loan Agreement, the lenders party thereto agreed to provide the Borrower with (i) a term loan facility in the aggregate principal amount of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_wpAg_pixNk6daaxK7TuvSw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_oYEZz4cGWkuBJQjXsczfDg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentFaceAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_MLK5IIc8F0qQonLVZ4ihsg">162.5</ix:nonFraction> million, deemed funded on the Closing Date and (ii) on an uncommitted and absolutely discretionary basis, a delayed draw term loan facility in a maximum aggregate amount of up to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_wpAg_pixNk6daaxK7TuvSw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_oYEZz4cGWkuBJQjXsczfDg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_EDjvpJRVBEanExQoPZ-oaA">175.0</ix:nonFraction> million, to be made available during the period from and including the Closing Date through and including the earliest to occur of (a) the date on which the delayed draw term loans have been fully drawn or (b) the date on which the discretionary delayed draw term loan commitments are terminated, subject to the satisfaction of certain conditions, each delayed draw term lender&#8217;s agreement, in its sole and absolute discretion, to provide a discretionary delayed draw term loan commitment thereunder, and Required Lenders (as defined in the Third Amended and Restated Credit Agreement) consent to such providing a discretionary delayed draw term loan commitment.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The maturity date of the 2026 Term Loan Agreement was extended to December 31, 2029. Until such maturity date, borrowings under the 2026 Term Loan Agreement shall bear interest at a rate per annum equal to a forward-looking term rate based on the Secured Overnight Financing Rate (&#8220;SOFR&#8221;)  for a tenor of three months (with a credit spread adjustment of </span><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_gRz7OzYGM0SBjvpvrLT5FQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:DebtInstrumentCreditSpreadAdjustmentOnVariableRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_1ZW5pGujc0SyT1BaaTdgIA">0.15</ix:nonFraction>% per annum) (or another applicable reference rate, as determined pursuant to the terms of the 2026 Term Loan Agreement) plus an applicable margin of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_gRz7OzYGM0SBjvpvrLT5FQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_ZSmTwMVYSkG13URD1JCUsw">6.50</ix:nonFraction>% (or, for ABR Loans, a base rate plus an applicable margin of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_VariableRateAxis_batl_AlternateBaseRateMember_X5oMaxUuQEybatIrcIiRFQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_O5D1NmWjxUy7WVmPu_grTw">5.50</ix:nonFraction>%). The applicable margin is fixed at <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_VariableRateAxis_us-gaap_SecuredOvernightFinancingRateSofrMember_tln8eqIltkGo3CR73W8jNg" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_LhI2DSdpr02QoGht8wXtPw">6.50</ix:nonFraction>% and replaces the leverage-based pricing grid contained in the 2024 </p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">17</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:36.7pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">BATTALION OIL CORPORATION</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">NOTES TO THE UNAUDITED CONDENSED CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS (continued)</b></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><a id="Tc_frZbbTXGnEiW8zfnqnyEOQ_1_0"></a><a id="Tc_Rr-d5lS1Q0O4U32xwo8zUA_1_3"></a><a id="Tc_J1jwksniYEmYAifoWgKAPQ_2_0"></a><a id="Tc_UQemfJwS2Ue0uatamq6n9Q_2_3"></a><a id="Tc_lCumxPlVD0-sgvfWlooIIw_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_DDB1NZoYtUyZhhbiKBNZZw_4_0"></a><ix:continuation id="Tb_Vc6cIfTtcUeJI6el0u8I8w_cont5" continuedAt="Tb_Vc6cIfTtcUeJI6el0u8I8w_cont6"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Amended Term Loan Agreement, under which the applicable SOFR margin ranged from <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_VariableRateAxis_us-gaap_SecuredOvernightFinancingRateSofrMember_Z1sGc3GP80S0xcx7thHacA" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:LineOfCreditFacilityCovenantComplianceTotalNetLeverageRatioRangeLowerRangeLimit" scale="0" id="Narr_FY2InDhKE0-OP36IJNPe-A">7.75</ix:nonFraction>% to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_VariableRateAxis_us-gaap_SecuredOvernightFinancingRateSofrMember_Z1sGc3GP80S0xcx7thHacA" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:LineOfCreditFacilityCovenantComplianceTotalNetLeverageRatioRangeUpperRangeLimit" scale="0" id="Narr_HmQ14L2mGkefp6ti0AKX_g">8.50</ix:nonFraction>% depending on the Total Net Leverage Ratio.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Entry into the 2026 Term Loan Agreement was accounted for as a modification and as such, the Company deferred an additional $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_wpAg_pixNk6daaxK7TuvSw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_oYEZz4cGWkuBJQjXsczfDg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DeferredFinanceCostsNet" scale="6" id="Narr_jt7ZJpnhI0-U33lvVl3H-w">0.4</ix:nonFraction> million of deferred financing costs at June 30, 2026 in conjunction with entry into the 2026 Term Loan Agreement to be amortized to interest expense using the straight-line method, which approximates the effective interest method, over the life of the debt.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:12pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Borrower may elect, at its option, to prepay any borrowing outstanding under the 2026 Term Loan Agreement. Such voluntary prepayments, certain mandatory prepayments and change of control prepayments are subject to the following prepayment premium, as applicable:</p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_LeqMErBSKUSMxTIrmvq7eA" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfDebtInstrumentsTextBlock" id="Tb_drC_wqP9l0-iGlB2Y0Gvow" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;min-height:0.0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:0pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:100%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:15.45%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:5.82%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:5.82%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:72.9%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:15.45%;background:#ffffff;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Period</b></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:5.82%;background:#ffffff;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-weight:bold;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:5.82%;background:#ffffff;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-weight:bold;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:72.9%;background:#ffffff;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Premium</b></p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:15.45%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">Months <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MinimumMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodAxis_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodOneMember_dVpmedjnlE-RD357a3nuyA" format="ixt-sec:durmonth" name="batl:DebtInstrumentPrepaymentTerm" id="Narr_h7RuhRzPWUKSEfW6EAppaA">0</ix:nonNumeric> - <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodAxis_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodOneMember_egs82-xXOkOBzibFspIePg" format="ixt-sec:durmonth" name="batl:DebtInstrumentPrepaymentTerm" id="Narr_v2GiPcZdQU6r3wo4dWQUTA">12</ix:nonNumeric></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:5.82%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:5.82%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:72.9%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.5pt 0pt 0pt;">Make-whole amount equal to 12 months of interest; provided that in the event of (a) a Change of Control Prepayment (as defined in the 2026 Term Loan Agreement) or (b) the sale of all or substantially all of the loan parties' assets, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodAxis_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodOneMember_aRCij4ilH0G6WCopH9sd_w" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:DebtInstrumentPrepaymentPremiumOverAccruedInterest" scale="-2" id="Narr_hbzwloMUCE2IwBSu3IYXrg">2.00</ix:nonFraction>%</p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:15.45%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">Months <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MinimumMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodAxis_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodTwoMember_cddTrQOB-UaqiIUIWmBxUw" format="ixt-sec:durmonth" name="batl:DebtInstrumentPrepaymentTerm" id="Narr_7Mvl5XBnuE-KPQ_JO7s_Rg">13</ix:nonNumeric> - <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodAxis_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodTwoMember_Ade_NKAl-Eu5O1nGa882Xw" format="ixt-sec:durmonth" name="batl:DebtInstrumentPrepaymentTerm" id="Narr_VvdLJNv5-EC3RV78W-U54g">24</ix:nonNumeric></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:5.82%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:5.82%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:72.9%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.5pt 0pt 0pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodAxis_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodTwoMember_U40HLrdTSk-xA_ENstw4tA" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:DebtInstrumentPrepaymentPremiumOverAccruedInterest" scale="-2" id="Tc_ZIXneXmkcUeNPA24q9n7nQ_3_3">1.00</ix:nonFraction>%</p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:15.45%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">Thereafter</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:5.82%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:5.82%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:72.9%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3.5pt 0pt 0pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodAxis_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentRedemptionPeriodThreeMember_d0vjyOl74kSCkotKAgs2Hw" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:DebtInstrumentPrepaymentPremiumOverAccruedInterest" scale="-2" id="Tc_f5GfiBA3VUGVYMsLZO_akA_4_3">0.00</ix:nonFraction>%</p></td></tr></table></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;min-height:0.0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:0pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:12pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Borrower may be required to make mandatory prepayments of the loans under the 2026 Term Loan Agreement in connection with the incurrence of non-permitted debt, certain asset sales and with excess cash on hand in excess of certain maximum levels. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:12pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Borrower is required to make scheduled amortization payments (i)&#160;commencing with the fiscal quarter ending June&#160;30, 2027 through and including the fiscal quarter ending March&#160;31, 2029, in an aggregate principal amount equal to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_batl_RatioToBeMaintainedForQuarterEndPeriodFromJune2027ThroughAndIncludingQuarterEndMarch2029Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_OIxsWP3vUUiGUx3eUn97aQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:DebtInstrumentQuarterlyAmortizationPaymentsPercent" scale="-2" id="Narr_bLCsALt0gEiMNaVqIHJE-g">1.25</ix:nonFraction>% of the loans outstanding on the Closing Date, (ii)&#160;for the fiscal quarter ending June&#160;30, 2029, an aggregate principal amount equal to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_batl_RatioToBeMaintainedForQuarterEndingPeriodJune2029Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_VyItCilMsUiei08xAOkFUg" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:DebtInstrumentQuarterlyAmortizationPaymentsPercent" scale="-2" id="Narr_1wwBUJx0mkulTe8L4GS19Q">7.50</ix:nonFraction>% of the loans outstanding on the Closing Date, and (iii)&#160;for the fiscal quarter ending September 30, 2029, an aggregate principal amount equal to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_batl_RatioToBeMaintainedForQuarterEndingPeriodSeptember2029Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_wbW1zwlo1U2Wz-EFHw90Iw" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:DebtInstrumentQuarterlyAmortizationPaymentsPercent" scale="-2" id="Narr_FFuSsUTc70eGERnx_5Dlbg">10.00</ix:nonFraction>% of the loans outstanding on the Closing Date.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Amounts outstanding under the 2026 Term Loan Agreement are guaranteed by certain of the Borrower&#8217;s direct and indirect subsidiaries and secured by a security interest in substantially all of the assets of the Borrower and such direct and indirect subsidiaries, and of the equity interests of the Borrower held by the Company. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 6pt 0pt;">The 2026 Term Loan agreement contains certain financial covenants (as defined in the 2026 Term Loan Agreement), including the maintenance of the following ratios:</p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:56.15pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Asset Coverage Ratio not to fall below </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MinimumMember_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_batl_RatioToBeMaintainedForQuarterEndPeriodFromSeptember2026ThroughAndIncludingQuarterEndDecember2026Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_IBRiZyNzjEaBwdOf-2HyZA" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:LineOfCreditFacilityCovenantAssetCoverageRatio" scale="-2" id="Narr_XOHOfpE7Bk-DAKLvY65G6A">1.75</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">x as of each fiscal quarter ending September 30, 2026 through and including December 31, 2026, </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_batl_RatioToBeMaintainedForQuarterEndPeriodFromMarch2027ThroughAndIncludingQuarterEndDecember2027Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_wtYlzhRmMUyaGOzz001y7A" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:LineOfCreditFacilityCovenantAssetCoverageRatio" scale="-2" id="Narr_bsf5zw-gJk2lfCfFaT01NQ">2.00</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">x as of each fiscal quarter ending March 31, 2027 through and including December 31, 2027 and </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_batl_RatioToBeMaintainedForQuarterEndPeriodFromJune2027ThroughAndIncludingQuarterEndMarch2029Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_qaIXYyAweES_dG10VyFgKA" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:LineOfCreditFacilityCovenantAssetCoverageRatio" scale="-2" id="Narr_Ua4Q-sY8YEO4PuS7LH34Ow">2.50</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">x for each fiscal quarter thereafter, determined as of the last day of each fiscal quarter;</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:56.15pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Total Net Leverage Ratio not to exceed </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_batl_RatioToBeMaintainedForQuarterEndPeriodFromSeptember2026ThroughAndIncludingQuarterEndDecember2026Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_rkEXo9vE9EKED4FHtPIs0w" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:LineOfCreditFacilityCovenantNetLeverageRatio" scale="-2" id="Narr_gbzqfGVBv06T7CGiWufmkQ">2.75</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">x as of each fiscal quarter ending September 30, 2026 through and including December 31, 2026 and </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_batl_RatioToBeMaintainedForEachQuarterAfterJune2026Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_rEL_1QI7TUStMp1S_E627A" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:LineOfCreditFacilityCovenantNetLeverageRatio" scale="-2" id="Narr_YL94pzsnh0G_j1eATIjEtg">2.50</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">x for each fiscal quarter thereafter, determined as of the last day of each fiscal quarter; </span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:56.15pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Current Ratio not to fall below </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_oYEZz4cGWkuBJQjXsczfDg" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:LineOfCreditFacilityCovenantCurrentRatio" scale="-2" id="Narr_yiJpR4kSoUG8qWerfdPUxg">1.00</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">x, determined as of the last day of any fiscal quarter commencing with the fiscal quarter ending September 30, 2026; and </span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:56.15pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Liquidity not to fall below the greater of (x) </span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_wpAg_pixNk6daaxK7TuvSw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_gRz7OzYGM0SBjvpvrLT5FQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:ThresholdLiquidityAmountToBeMaintained" scale="0" id="Narr_mVAMyYpH-kS4YQUN0Q8_DQ">10,000,000</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"> and (y) the amount equal to the scheduled principal and interest payments for the immediately succeeding three-month period, determined as of the last day of any fiscal quarter.</span></td></tr></table><div style="margin-top:6pt;"></div></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">18</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:36.7pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">BATTALION OIL CORPORATION</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">NOTES TO THE UNAUDITED CONDENSED CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS (continued)</b></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_Vc6cIfTtcUeJI6el0u8I8w_cont6"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt;">Under the 2026 Term Loan Agreement, the Company continues to be required to hedge approximately <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_FUS0H_atvUeN7Ebzq4u_Xw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:DebtInstrumentCollateralHedgedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_p65BTBqeoUSR6qyLFOD22w">85</ix:nonFraction>% to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure__HAJHAyJfkuHxmsBxJ_Eww" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MinimumMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_batl_TermLoanCreditAgreement2026Member_R9pR3Gmjo0CzGlnWpESJUg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="batl:DebtInstrumentCollateralHedgedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_zDqkHV_izk-Qg94wrhf2iQ">50</ix:nonFraction>% of its anticipated oil and natural gas production, in varying percentages by year, on a rolling basis for the next four years. The 2026 Term Loan Agreement also contains certain events of default, including non-payment; breaches of representations and warranties; non-compliance with covenants or other agreements; cross-default to material indebtedness; judgments; change of control; and voluntary and involuntary bankruptcy.<span style="white-space:pre-wrap;">  </span></p></ix:continuation><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><a id="_contentSection_41c2b2b4_3992_4029_a996_"></a><a id="_f59c9b98_4da6_4346_9d77_e1adf89d3316"></a><a id="_f59c9b98_4da6_4346_9d77_e1adf89d3316_2"></a><a id="_f59c9b98_4da6_4346_9d77_e1adf89d3316_3"></a><a id="_b5ec5359_9adb_44b2_aafd_f95593e58e56"></a><a id="Tc_TxVTfUJnlEiQ60CL3v6IiQ_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_lTngdBXcgEWxCbs9uOJSOw_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_D6ccJGrWx0GejbxoDz8Rxw_2_5"></a><a id="Tc_mHk6o8f_Qkqu0jc9MwQU4Q_2_8"></a><a id="Tc_vB8b2RqFmUCl4VtnQElGmQ_2_11"></a><a id="Tc_gP-XtDKqf0OCtxujd_ZtdA_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_DiVawtn7Y0S9rxsm2eM7FQ_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_kx3s1v_yBU2TiZwIcL7iiA_4_2"></a><a id="Tc_Mr7UFm4Bd0WBPZ9Z85MXAw_4_3"></a><a id="Tc_3-sZ7M13cUqYWhnLDZDiMA_4_5"></a><a id="Tc_L2_tjxjBqUG994AGRGFReQ_4_8"></a><a id="Tc_mggF6NhvH06b8OZmpooqgQ_4_9"></a><a id="Tc_5-dyeAP7xECQmZe2akJj7Q_4_11"></a><a id="Tc_r4IP-v3o5kK_M4SrZ9rGFQ_6_0"></a><a id="Tc_mZr5hMu93UWOEYC7ySryGA_7_0"></a><a id="Tc_ipjLrcr9KEK1NbukILgz0A_7_2"></a><a id="Tc_FtC6FV-nbUCZnJ0Htzsl2Q_7_3"></a><a id="Tc_6kadiR2mVE-3sobzBQrcxw_7_5"></a><a id="Tc_0K4EVPUfhEevFNLIISKs-g_7_8"></a><a id="Tc_NyCdlD8i3Ea7WWfdxkameQ_7_9"></a><a id="Tc_t4LK4JBRvUi5dS0e6zkQng_7_11"></a><a id="_eb88bb84_df23_4c51_82c2_62dc37412ae8"></a><a id="Tc_ulWrwKmY1kupg1WgUWHmLg_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_0Ay5f6T0BUqerXfWZ84z6w_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_jsbyiVQQ1E20Xw9WpwVFgQ_2_5"></a><a id="Tc_YTYhmidVnUaOboLGLuPXew_2_8"></a><a id="Tc_WzcELyn5IkW_Xn1mDnul6g_2_11"></a><a id="Tc_qfIEWJFajkqWcjsELQ9HtQ_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_z1ruRe_nfU2Mr-hNeyY21w_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_jUNkNQ8iZkGDJ2lGoCFwKw_4_2"></a><a id="Tc_P1MBKcqwsUKWtxYxhRv3Dw_4_3"></a><a id="Tc_juSCOZYU50C4ljal8qqxBw_4_5"></a><a id="Tc_zYsvYlLXHkSvmSwy5cW8eg_4_8"></a><a id="Tc_6dznp7gZOUi0QQMZGGzzkw_4_9"></a><a id="Tc_C3fBVjvssEePFsUEIwkYxQ_4_11"></a><a id="Tc_jV-LSW712kKhmcA6KCshMA_6_0"></a><a id="Tc_KUORd3OvxUW3tUhJgSywsA_7_0"></a><a id="Tc_v1CJdrjsbEKpn3oSOMmCSA_7_2"></a><a id="Tc_sdTYQjS7e0mjIHsy8LhllA_7_3"></a><a id="Tc_srq4oeF__ESCb2XEuZiAHQ_7_5"></a><a id="Tc_2CCU4QlijUi8lyTiNA6WwA_7_8"></a><a id="Tc_lp_8VN7xrU6vU8ifAm6rkg_7_9"></a><a id="Tc_z8_XY5jOHk2_z0pbfx7Obw_7_11"></a><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_LeqMErBSKUSMxTIrmvq7eA" name="us-gaap:FairValueDisclosuresTextBlock" id="Tb_EvcdXrRBg02x_Acx-fIgyA" continuedAt="Tb_EvcdXrRBg02x_Acx-fIgyA_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">6. FAIR VALUE MEASUREMENTS</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company&#8217;s determination of fair value incorporates not only the credit standing of the counterparties involved in transactions with the Company resulting in receivables on the Company&#8217;s unaudited condensed consolidated balance sheets, but also the impact of the Company&#8217;s nonperformance risk on its own liabilities. Fair value is defined as the price that would be received to sell an asset or paid to transfer a liability in an orderly transaction between market participants at the measurement date (exit price). The Company separates the fair value of its financial instruments using a fair value hierarchy that prioritizes the inputs to valuation techniques used to measure fair value. The hierarchy assigns the highest priority to unadjusted quoted prices in active markets for identical assets or liabilities (Level&#160;1) and the lowest priority to unobservable inputs (Level&#160;3). Level&#160;2 measurements are inputs that are observable for assets or liabilities, either directly or indirectly, other than quoted prices included within Level&#160;1. The Company utilizes market data or assumptions that market participants would use in pricing the asset or liability, including assumptions about risk and the risks inherent in the inputs to the valuation technique. These inputs can be readily observable, market corroborated, or generally unobservable. The Company classifies fair value balances based on the observability of those inputs.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 6pt 0pt;">A financial instrument&#8217;s level within the fair value hierarchy is based on the lowest level of input that is significant to the fair value measurement. The Company&#8217;s assessment of the significance of a particular input to the fair value measurement requires judgment, and may affect the valuation of fair value assets and liabilities and their placement within the fair value hierarchy levels. There were <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_wpAg_pixNk6daaxK7TuvSw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_LeqMErBSKUSMxTIrmvq7eA" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="batl:FairValueMeasurementAssetTransfersBetweenLevels" scale="3" id="Narr_oeQ0yO_C10yzs7kbKesR2A"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_wpAg_pixNk6daaxK7TuvSw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_Up6keKHLxUKDR22Mp9nj1g" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="batl:FairValueMeasurementAssetTransfersBetweenLevels" scale="3" id="Narr_WrjYKf8makyVjLwHnEKj-w">no</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> transfers between fair value hierarchy levels for any period presented. <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_LeqMErBSKUSMxTIrmvq7eA" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfFairValueAssetsAndLiabilitiesMeasuredOnRecurringBasisTableTextBlock" id="Group_fUor2tmIBUio9S9yiTNeMg" continuedAt="Group_fUor2tmIBUio9S9yiTNeMg_2" escape="true">The following tables set forth by level within the fair value hierarchy the Company&#8217;s financial assets and liabilities associated with commodity-based derivative contracts that were accounted for at fair value at June 30, 2026 and December 31, 2025 (in thousands):</ix:nonNumeric></p><ix:continuation id="Group_fUor2tmIBUio9S9yiTNeMg_2"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;min-height:0.0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:0pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:100%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:54.89%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.98%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.25%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;<